# Docs Snippet Workflow

## Source of truth

SDK example code lives in the SDK trees:

- `sdks/python/examples/`
- `sdks/typescript/src/v1/examples/`
- `sdks/go/examples/`
- `sdks/ruby/examples/`

The mirrors under `examples/{lang}/` are **generated** from those trees. Never
edit generated mirrors directly; edit the SDK copy and regenerate.

Exception: `examples/*/guides/` is not generated (the old `sdks/guides/`
source tree no longer exists). Guide files are hand-maintained — edit them in
place.

## Snippet markers

Use `# > Step Title` (or `// >` for TS/Go) to open a snippet and `# !!`
(or `// !!`) to close it. The generator converts the title to snake_case for
the snippet key (e.g. `# > Simple Step Retries` → `simple_step_retries`).
Markers are stripped from the generated mirrors.

## Regenerating

After editing any example under `sdks/`, run from the repo root:

```
task generate-docs
```

(or directly: `cd frontend/snippets && python -X utf8 generate.py`, using the
repo `.venv`). This regenerates the `examples/{lang}/` mirrors and
`frontend/docs/lib/generated/snippets/index.ts`, then formats the output.

## Referencing snippets in MDX

```
snippets.{lang}.{example_dir}.{file_stem}.{snippet_key}
```
